      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'ever notice that christians are bad drivers' because the meme uses an interrogative tone ('ever notice') that implicitly invites the viewer to consider or acknowledge the stereotype, making the user feel personally addressed or prompted to reflect on the claim. This creates a semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the one who might 'notice' or be aware of the stereotype.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
